  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Resources for Health Development and Retention</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tanzania):  On September 30, 2022, the HRH Development and Retention activity transitioned the WISN-POA platform to the GOT. The WISN-POA platform -- including the bottom-up planning database and allocation tool  -- ensures the health workforce is rationalized to provide support where it is most needed among GOT hospitals. The FY2022 funds will tailor and test the WISN-POA platform for use by the 105 Christian Social Services Commission hospitals owned by the Tanzania Episcopal Conference and Christian Council of Tanzania members. These faith-based hospitals provide 40 percent of the maternal and child health services in the country. The increased utilization of the WISN-POA platform will ensure that the national healthcare workforce is distributed more rationally and efficiently. Note: This activity is also receiving HIV HSS funds...</narrative>
  </description>
